+# Native risk-title-only home Alpha continuation
+
+This separate opt-in policy admits only the actual unit71 title alert for `lem-incompressible-surface-torus-boundary-essential-or-parallel-annulus`. It creates one ordinary owner gate obligation, never a fabricated reader/refuter finding or inherited verdict. The old16 plus new gate are all independently owed, with full current risk review. Foreign-refuter and unit67 escalation rules are unchanged.
+
+The registry is `research/RUN-step3-native-risk-title-home-alpha-continuations.json`, version1, policy `owner-step3-native-risk-title-home-alpha-continuation-v1`, authorized_by `owner`, explicit authorization, exactly one continuation. The isolated test fixture provides a complete schema example; it is synthetic test evidence, never a registry to install. No helper writes a registry, source, state, native report or decision.
+
+Each entry binds unit71, root ownership, fixed native-risk-title continuation label, canonical batch71, no mathematical acceptance or inherited acceptance, actual writer-drain time, immutable native result/attempt/prompt, archived original report/16decisions/scope/risk contract, exact source and manifest before/after archives, genuine root two-file application and bounded title-only review, honest root artifact capture, the actual native alert quotation, unique defect_id, task ref and all current home input raw hashes. References are run-local research paths with SHA256; symlinks, escaping/nonregular paths and changed evidence reject. Original native completion authenticates output paths, not structured report bytes; the required capture explicitly says the latter are not native-byte-attested.
+
+Root must capture actual preimages before editing. The only admitted source delta is the unique top-level single-line frontmatter title replaced with `title: "Boundary-compressible incompressible surfaces at torus boundary are parallel annuli"`. All other bytes, including Statement/Definition/proof/deps/metadata, stay identical. The parsed manifest changes only the unique target title mirror; order, pages, metadata and every other field remain identical. The target retains exactly one actual home. The original target was high-risk/untouched, never an old owed decision. The pre3a snapshot must remain absent; do not create one to manufacture extra obligations.
+
+Before selected dispatch, old canonical outputs still equal archived preimages and every actual current input matches its seal. Any completed new-label attempt, including failure, spends the one-shot route. The real wrapper checks before the ordinary planner can write a task, preserves other units, substitutes only this result label and assembles the registered task with the ordinary task. Doctor planning writes no assembled task. The delivered native task must explicitly contain all16 old obligations, the new gate, canonical outputs/identity, no inherited acceptance and full current risk review.
+
+Fresh native outputs require all17 exact ordinary routes and IDs. The new gate carries exactly its real defect_id and an ordinary independent verdict, never context_accepted. Escalations and uncertain repairs remain blocking. A fresh complete target risk review needs meaningful new notes and no unresolved alert. Ordinary native ledger, carrier checks, stamp, post3a and closure remain mandatory; this policy supplies neither mathematical acceptance nor gate passage.
+
+Active Step3 validates the approved live source/manifest carrier and fresh risk closure. Historical verification permits later legitimate owner repairs only when the v3 closed receipt freezes this exact registry, all historical refs (including source/manifest after archives), fresh native stable/attempt/prompt, and canonical fresh report/decisions at their raw hashes. A bare closed marker or mismatched artifact is rejected. Ordinary step3-close verifies the entire frozen receipt, ledger and artifact set; this bounded historical test does not replace it.
+
+## Installation and reload (root only)
+
+After independent acceptance and unit71 writer drain, root verifies the integration preimages and installs the reviewed patch, performs the actual two-file title edit/capture/review, registers truthful evidence/task/current inputs and runs the required installed suites. Do not fabricate pending application fields or timestamps.
+
+The wrapper propagates its import query to the home helper. The parent mathlib module caches Step3 by Step3 file mtime/size, so wrapper editing alone does not ensure a fresh closure. After installation root deliberately refreshes `tools/autopilot/stages/mathlib.step3.mts` mtime with `touch` (no content/state change), then uses the existing native guarded reload. Verify the actual `stages-reloaded` event/new stage epoch and unchanged durable completed prefix/units before continuing. This is not a global restart requirement or permission to mutate engine state. Relevant unit71 writers must be drained; root owns native controls.
+
+Tests exercise real TS wrapper doctor/plan/pattern/task assembly, native authorResultAllowed, before-writer rejection, old/new obligations, exact title/manifest limits, one-shot failure, fresh outputs/risk, frozen historical evidence and unchanged no-opt-in policies. Existing home and unit67 regression suites use explicit import-closure overlays, including the new module and the root's already-active dependency-order helper; that helper itself is unchanged here.
